{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For.</b> He will growl, like the meaning of \"he will roar.\"" "<b>that are called.</b> One to another, to join together to do battle with the lion." "<b>in fullness.</b> All of them, so that no shepherd is lacking who does not come." "<b>and though they are tumultuous, he will not respond.</b> From the root of ענה (Deuteronomy 24:12), and also לענות (Exodus 10:3), and like it: זמיר עריצים יענה (Isaiah 25:5)." "<b>will come down.</b> An allusion to the angel."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {3 "The root reference ענה in Deuteronomy 24:12 is תענה; Ibn Ezra cites it by root. Exodus 10:3 citation reads לענות in some witnesses; resolving as cited."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:12.655988218Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}